{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1538511-curseborne-sorcerers-linage-what-s-their-story-mechanics","id":1538511,"title":"[Curseborne] Sorcerers Linage - What's their story & mechanics?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-13T04:19:36-07:00","id":1538511,"title":"[Curseborne] Sorcerers Linage - What's their story & mechanics?","content":"So I like how Sorcerers are 'addicted to magic' and they have 'eating disorder on casting magic'. When they lose all Curse Dice, they NEED to cast magic, until they Sacrifice things they Family point to. They WANTED to have magic so much - they are Cursed all they time, on they own wanting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> More to listen on design decision by Danielle for Sorcerers from 45:00 till 51:00 of this Pathcast -<br /> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ew/pb-eybr9-1666dcc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.podbean.com/ew/pb-eybr9-1666dcc</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-13-2024, 07:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T06:07:28-07:00","id":1538513,"title":"","content":"From what I've gleaned, they have the opposite problem than most wizards in urban fantasy. They aren't a few and often dying breed, they are living wellsprings of change and chaos...and it is constantly trying to spew out lest it burn them out. Their Curse Dice isn't fuel, they're stoppers on the flow. <br /> <br /> Hence, greed for more magic vs. self-control of managing the magic you have...and which actually sells the idea of an evil wizard who seeks only knowledge better than just &quot;curiosity am evil&quot; (it isn't, but a Sorcerer who cares only about increasing power is a Sorcerer who clearly does not give a frog's ass about the sheer destruction it can cause, and continues to cause).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T07:33:17-07:00","id":1538562,"title":"","content":"In terms of mechanics, it was mentioned that magic system will be similar to the one found in At The Gates. Since I backed it and have access to the manuscript, I wrote down a brief description of the magic system found in ATG and posted it on <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/onyx-path-curseborne.912035/page-74#post-25242066\" target=\"_blank\">rpg.net</a>. I don't want to cross-post but feel free to read it if you're interested in the (potential) mechanical side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28450-dominikd","name":"DominikD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}